{"id": "573393184776f41900660da6", "title": "University_of_Notre_Dame", "context": "The Rev. Theodore Hesburgh, C.S.C., (1917\u20132015) served as president for 35 years (1952\u201387) of dramatic transformations. In that time the annual operating budget rose by a factor of 18 from $9.7 million to $176.6 million, and the endowment by a factor of 40 from $9 million to $350 million, and research funding by a factor of 20 from $735,000 to $15 million. Enrollment nearly doubled from 4,979 to 9,600, faculty more than doubled 389 to 950, and degrees awarded annually doubled from 1,212 to 2,500.", "question": "What was the lifespan of Theodore Hesburgh?", "answers": {"text": ["1917\u20132015"], "answer_start": [37]}}
