{"id": "5733e0d64776f419006613fc", "title": "Anthropology", "context": "Cyborg anthropology originated as a sub-focus group within the American Anthropological Association's annual meeting in 1993. The sub-group was very closely related to STS and the Society for the Social Studies of Science. Donna Haraway's 1985 Cyborg Manifesto could be considered the founding document of cyborg anthropology by first exploring the philosophical and sociological ramifications of the term. Cyborg anthropology studies humankind and its relations with the technological systems it has built, specifically modern technological systems that have reflexively shaped notions of what it means to be human beings.", "question": "What type of anthropology originated as a sub-focus group?", "answers": {"text": ["Cyborg"], "answer_start": [0]}}
