{"id": "573363724776f41900660995", "title": "Financial_crisis_of_2007%E2%80%9308", "context": "Stock trader and financial risk engineer Nassim Nicholas Taleb, author of the 2007 book The Black Swan, spent years warning against the breakdown of the banking system in particular and the economy in general owing to their use of bad risk models and reliance on forecasting, and their reliance on bad models, and framed the problem as part of \"robustness and fragility\". He also took action against the establishment view by making a big financial bet on banking stocks and making a fortune from the crisis (\"They didn't listen, so I took their money\"). According to David Brooks from the New York Times, \"Taleb not only has an explanation for what\u2019s happening, he saw it coming.\"", "question": "Who wrote the 2007 book The Black Swan?", "answers": {"text": ["Nassim Nicholas Taleb"], "answer_start": [41]}}
