{"id": "573366a64776f419006609fd", "title": "Saint_Barth%C3%A9lemy", "context": "Located approximately 250 kilometres (160 mi) east of Puerto Rico and the nearer Virgin Islands, St. Barth\u00e9lemy lies immediately southeast of the islands of Saint Martin and Anguilla. It is one of the Renaissance Islands. St. Barth\u00e9lemy is separated from Saint Martin by the Saint-Barth\u00e9lemy Channel. It lies northeast of Saba and St Eustatius, and north of St Kitts. Some small satellite islets belong to St. Barth\u00e9lemy including \u00cele Chevreau (\u00cele Bonhomme), \u00cele Fr\u00e9gate, \u00cele Toc Vers, \u00cele Tortue and Gros \u00celets (\u00celots Syndare). A much bigger islet, \u00cele Fourchue, lies on the north of the island, in the Saint-Barth\u00e9lemy Channel. Other rocky islets which include Coco, the Roques (or little Turtle rocks), the Goat, and the Sugarloaf.", "question": "How many Miles East of Puerto Rico is St. Barts?", "answers": {"text": ["160"], "answer_start": [38]}}
