{"id": "56de4796cffd8e1900b4b777", "title": "Symbiosis", "context": "The biologist Lynn Margulis, famous for her work on endosymbiosis, contends that symbiosis is a major driving force behind evolution. She considers Darwin's notion of evolution, driven by competition, to be incomplete and claims that evolution is strongly based on co-operation, interaction, and mutual dependence among organisms. According to Margulis and Dorion Sagan, \"Life did not take over the globe by combat, but by networking.\"", "question": "What does Margulis think is the main driver of evolution?", "answers": {"text": ["symbiosis"], "answer_start": [56]}}
