{"id": "56df95d44a1a83140091eb7e", "title": "Lighting", "context": "For example, in order to meet the expectations for good color rendering in retail applications, research suggests using the well-established CRI along with another metric called gamut area index (GAI). GAI represents the relative separation of object colors illuminated by a light source; the greater the GAI, the greater the apparent saturation or vividness of the object colors. As a result, light sources which balance both CRI and GAI are generally preferred over ones that have only high CRI or only high GAI.", "question": "What does GAI stand for?", "answers": {"text": ["gamut area index"], "answer_start": [178]}}
