{"id": "56dfa4514a1a83140091ec06", "title": "Hunter-gatherer", "context": "At the 1966 \"Man the Hunter\" conference, anthropologists Richard Borshay Lee and Irven DeVore suggested that egalitarianism was one of several central characteristics of nomadic hunting and gathering societies because mobility requires minimization of material possessions throughout a population. Therefore, no surplus of resources can be accumulated by any single member. Other characteristics Lee and DeVore proposed were flux in territorial boundaries as well as in demographic composition.", "question": "At what conference did Richard Borshay speak?", "answers": {"text": ["Man the Hunter"], "answer_start": [13]}}
